      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Troubleshooting",
        "Correction controls"
      ],
      "text": "Correction controls",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 16,
        "line": 19,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Troubleshooting",
        "Correction controls"
      ],
      "text": "Since 2026-09-01, employees can submit their own attendance correction requests within 14 calendar days of the workday if payroll is unlocked. Approval remains with the manager and triggers recalculation within five minutes. ATT-409 means a pending correction already exists; withdraw it before submitting a replacement. ATT-LOCK routes to HR Payroll. A request outside the window also requires HR Payroll review. Attendance Correction Guide v1's direct manager-edit procedure is historical and must not be used to bypass these controls.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 17,
        "line": 21,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Troubleshooting",
        "Investigation evidence"
      ],
      "text": "Investigation evidence",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": null,
      "is_semantic": true,
      "list_level": null,
      "location": {
        "bbox": null,
        "element": 18,
        "line": 22,
        "page": null,
        "part": null
      },
      "marker": null,
      "ordered": null,
      "rows": null,
      "section_path": [
        "Attendance Troubleshooting",
        "Investigation evidence"
      ],
      "text": "Provide the affected date, timezone, visible event sequence, latest calculation state, correction request status, and exact error code. Do not attach unrelated team attendance or a full payroll statement. If approval succeeded but recalculation failed, support investigates the linked calculation job while HR retains the approved request. Do not edit another workday to compensate, and do not approve an overtime award against a known incorrect total.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
